## Objective

Implement durable, passive c2c ingress for an active app-server-managed Codex
thread. Persist the message in the canonical broker inbox first, then make that
same message model-visible through the T001-validated `thread/inject_items`
request. Delivery is exactly-once when acknowledgement or history
reconciliation can prove acceptance; the explicitly tested ambiguous-ack
window is otherwise observable at-least-once. This task must never start,
steer, interrupt, or approve a turn.

## Scope and non-goals

- Consume canonical local-broker messages for the managed identity supplied by
  T002 and inject a data-only Codex history item into its loaded thread.
- Own durable delivery state, retries, reconnect/reload handling, bounded
  backpressure, idempotency, and fallback to existing hook/poll delivery.
- Preserve DM/room envelope, sender attribution, `message_id`, timestamps,
  deferrable metadata, and existing ephemeral/archive semantics.
- This task does **not** call `turn/start` (T007), inspect or decide composer/DND
  wake policy (T007), add public commands (T006), or change approval handling.
- Do not use PTY writes, `tmux send-keys`, Herdr pane execution,
  `turn/steer`, or `turn/interrupt` under any condition.

